 "final_text": "**CESP February close \u2014 root cause found and answer submitted.**\n\n- **AR subledger: tied.** ERP (CustomerTransactions, dataareaid `CESP`, 3 open Feb invoices) sums to **$128,500.00**, matching the recon workbook exactly. Status: \"tied.\"\n- **AP subledger: not tied \u2014 this is the blocker.** ERP (VendorTransactions, dataareaid `CESP`) sums to **$80,500.00** (3 open Feb vendor invoices: $28,000 + $19,500 + $33,000), but the recon workbook shows only **$78,000.00**, status \"in progress.\" Variance = **$2,500.00** (workbook is short vs. ERP).\n- **Owner:** Per the Month-End Close Checklist (FIN-SOP-001), task #3 \"AP subledger tie-out\" is owned by **Jordan Blake** (same person listed as preparer on the workbook row still marked \"in progress\"). No email escalation thread exists yet, so this hasn't been flagged beyond the workbook status.\n\nSubmitted:\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| erp_ar_balance | 128,500.00 |\n| erp_ap_balance | 80,500.00 |\n| unreconciled_subledger | AP |\n| variance_amount | 2,500.00 |\n| blocking_task_owner | Jordan Blake |\n\nLikely next step for Jordan: one AP invoice (~$2,500) posted in the ERP for CESP in Feb isn't reflected in the recon workbook yet \u2014 worth checking `CFAP-01/02/03` against what was pulled into the workbook.",
